    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d136">

                <pb facs="0303" n="189" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg189"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00R296/4905: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Atherton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-08-10T22:00:00+01:00">August 10, 1931—10
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 10—7:55 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>330. From Livesey. Belgium has annexed its German Mark Agreement to the committee
                    report by the following footnote to paragraph 2: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The Belgian Government while willingly agreeing to President Hoover’s
                            proposal was obliged to reserve the question of the payments to be made
                            by Germany in fulfillment of the Marks Agreement dated July 13, 1929. An
                            agreement has been arrived at on this point between the two Governments
                            which has been embodied in an exchange of letters herewith
                                annexed.”<anchor n="77" xml:id="d136-f1"/></p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Atherton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d136-f1" n="77" xml:id="d136-f1-content">
                <p>See paragraph No. 9 of the final report of the International Committee of
                    Experts, Great Britain, Cmd. 3947, Misc. No. 19 (1931), p. 5.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
